{:edb/db-before-t 1481 :edb/db-after-t 1482 :edb/tx-data [[13194139534794 50 #inst "2026-10-08T07:06:22.242Z" 13194139534794 true] [17592186100801 1020 #edb/ref 17592186310495 13194139534794 true] [17592186100801 1020 #edb/ref 17592186310502 13194139534794 true] [17592186100801 1020 #edb/ref 17592186310509 13194139534794 true] [17592186100868 1020 #edb/ref 17592186310516 13194139534794 true] [17592186100868 1020 #edb/ref 17592186310523 13194139534794 true] [17592186100868 1020 #edb/ref 17592186310530 13194139534794 true] [17592186100868 1020 #edb/ref 17592186310538 13194139534794 true] [17592186101068 1100 "Consider the following differential equation.\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=\\frac{4y}{x},\\,x\\ne 0\n$$\n\n \n\nLet $f(x)={x}^{4}.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\n- ${f}^{′}(x)=5{x}^{5}.$\n- Substituting $y=f(x)$ and ${y}^{′}={f}^{′}(x)$ into the differential equation gives a true statement.\n- The function $y=f(x)$ is a solution of the differential equation." 13194139534794 true] [17592186101068 1100 "Consider the following differential equation.\n\n$y^{\\prime } = \\frac{4y}{x}, x \\ne 0$\n\nLet $f(x) = x^{4}$. Which of the following statements are true?\n\n1. $f^{\\prime }(x) = 5x^{5}$.\n2. Substituting $y = f(x)$ and $y^{\\prime } = f^{\\prime }(x)$ into the differential equation gives a true statement.\n3. The function $y = f(x)$ is a solution of the differential equation." 13194139534794 false] [17592186101068 1145 "Differentiate $f(x)=x^4$: $f'(x)=4x^3$, so statement I is false. For $x\\ne0$,\n$$\\frac{4f(x)}x=\\frac{4x^4}x=4x^3=f'(x).$$\nThe substitution is an identity, so II and III are true. The answer is **II and III only**." 13194139534794 false] [17592186101068 1145 "For a function $f(x)$ to be a solution to a differential equation, it must satisfy the equation for all values of $x$ in the equation's domain.\n\nWith that in mind, let's check each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is false. Differentiating $f(x)={x}^{4},$ we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =({x}^{4})^{′} \\\\  & =4{x}^{3} \\\\  & \\ne 5{x}^{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement II is true. Substituting $y={x}^{4}$ and ${y}^{′}=4{x}^{3}$ into the original equation, we get a true statement:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′} & \\overset{?}{=}\\frac{4y}{x} \\\\ (4{x}^{3}) & \\overset{?}{=}\\frac{4({x}^{4})}{x} \\\\ 4{x}^{3} & =4{x}^{3}\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement III is true. Since statement II is true, the function $y={x}^{4}$ is a solution to our differential equation.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\"" 13194139534794 true] [17592186281454 1000 #edb/ref 17592186310537 13194139534794 true] [17592186310495 1017 #edb/ref 17592186310496 13194139534794 true] [17592186310495 1089 "q-141080" 13194139534794 true] [17592186310495 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534794 true] [17592186310495 1100 "Consider the following differential equation.\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=2y\n$$\n\n \n\nLet $f(x)=\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\n- ${f}^{′}(x)=2\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x$\n- Substituting $y=f(x)$ and ${y}^{′}={f}^{′}(x)$ into the differential equation gives a true statement\n- The function $y=f(x)$ is a solution of the differential equation" 13194139534794 true] [17592186310495 1113 #uuid "3c5d8fd2-fb66-5109-b8f5-6406e18d1fe6" 13194139534794 true] [17592186310495 1145 "For a function $f(x)$ to be a solution to a differential equation, it must satisfy the equation for all values of $x$ in the equation's domain.\n\nWith that in mind, let's check each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is false. Differentiating $f(x)=\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x,$ we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & ={(\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x)}^{′} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 2\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x \\\\  & \\ne 2\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement II is false. Substituting $y=\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x$ and ${y}^{′}=\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x$ into the original equation, we get a false statement:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′} & \\overset{?}{=}2y \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡2x & \\overset{?}{=}2(\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x) \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡2x & \\ne \\operatorname{sin}⁡2x\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement III is false. Since statement II is false, the function $y=\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x$ is not a solution to our differential equation.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"None.\"" 13194139534794 true] [17592186310496 1000 #edb/ref 17592186310497 13194139534794 true] [17592186310496 1000 #edb/ref 17592186310498 13194139534794 true] [17592186310496 1000 #edb/ref 17592186310499 13194139534794 true] [17592186310496 1000 #edb/ref 17592186310500 13194139534794 true] [17592186310496 1000 #edb/ref 17592186310501 13194139534794 true] [17592186310496 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534794 true] [17592186310496 1041 "selection" 13194139534794 true] [17592186310496 1104 #edb/ref 17592186310500 13194139534794 true] [17592186310496 1110 #uuid "44b7284a-24a3-59f0-acf0-ff9f993c64d1" 13194139534794 true] [17592186310497 1034 "II and III only" 13194139534794 true] [17592186310497 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534794 true] [17592186310497 1111 #uuid "c0f8d466-522b-5e38-8b40-10106f232e20" 13194139534794 true] [17592186310498 1034 "I only" 13194139534794 true] [17592186310498 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534794 true] [17592186310498 1111 #uuid "d43b4b10-8063-5466-be3a-a3c3af6b66cd" 13194139534794 true] [17592186310499 1034 "III only" 13194139534794 true] [17592186310499 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534794 true] [17592186310499 1111 #uuid "e002db91-eb89-5d8f-867f-e2b8d1fe3b76" 13194139534794 true] [17592186310500 1034 "None" 13194139534794 true] [17592186310500 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534794 true] [17592186310500 1111 #uuid "30059b5a-4016-5fc7-8da6-22330210c414" 13194139534794 true] [17592186310501 1034 "II only" 13194139534794 true] [17592186310501 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534794 true] [17592186310501 1111 #uuid "e092af6a-ef57-5a2a-bda8-9a05223e717d" 13194139534794 true] [17592186310502 1017 #edb/ref 17592186310503 13194139534794 true] [17592186310502 1089 "q-141082" 13194139534794 true] [17592186310502 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534794 true] [17592186310502 1100 "Consider the following differential equation.\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=\\frac{1}{{e}^{y}}\n$$\n\n \n\nLet $f(x)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡x.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\n- ${f}^{′}(x)=\\frac{1}{x}$\n- Substituting $y=f(x)$ and ${y}^{′}={f}^{′}(x)$ into the differential equation gives a true statement\n- The function $y=f(x)$ is a solution of the differential equation" 13194139534794 true] [17592186310502 1113 #uuid "90a72911-f2a4-5e18-9c98-33431b3777b9" 13194139534794 true] [17592186310502 1145 "For a function $f(x)$ to be a solution to a differential equation, it must satisfy the equation for all values of $x$ in the equation's domain.\n\nWith that in mind, let's check each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. Differentiating $f(x)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡x,$ we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & ={(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)}^{′} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement II is true. Substituting $y=\\operatorname{ln}⁡x$ and ${y}^{′}=\\frac{1}{x}$ into the original equation, we get a true statement:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′} & \\overset{?}{=}\\frac{1}{{e}^{y}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{x} & \\overset{?}{=}\\frac{1}{{e}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{x} & =\\frac{1}{x}\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement III is true. Since statement II is true, the function $y=\\operatorname{ln}⁡x$ is a solution to our differential equation.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I, II, and III.\"" 13194139534794 true] [17592186310503 1000 #edb/ref 17592186310504 13194139534794 true] [17592186310503 1000 #edb/ref 17592186310505 13194139534794 true] [17592186310503 1000 #edb/ref 17592186310506 13194139534794 true] [17592186310503 1000 #edb/ref 17592186310507 13194139534794 true] [17592186310503 1000 #edb/ref 17592186310508 13194139534794 true] [17592186310503 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534794 true] [17592186310503 1041 "selection" 13194139534794 true] [17592186310503 1104 #edb/ref 17592186310504 13194139534794 true] [17592186310503 1110 #uuid "140c983c-b009-5108-b1e0-38503d18bbf0" 13194139534794 true] [17592186310504 1034 "I, II, and III" 13194139534794 true] [17592186310504 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534794 true] [17592186310504 1111 #uuid "f544ad4c-287f-5f45-bf2b-4ef526b966c2" 13194139534794 true] [17592186310505 1034 "II and III only" 13194139534794 true] [17592186310505 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534794 true] [17592186310505 1111 #uuid "cf8f82be-8027-57f2-bd5a-4060f0575094" 13194139534794 true] [17592186310506 1034 "I only" 13194139534794 true] [17592186310506 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534794 true] [17592186310506 1111 #uuid "f4965f74-f800-520e-9e40-e0efcb2f4993" 13194139534794 true] [17592186310507 1034 "III only" 13194139534794 true] [17592186310507 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534794 true] [17592186310507 1111 #uuid "ca1aaf8e-926d-59d2-8b66-4e1ff4215aa7" 13194139534794 true] [17592186310508 1034 "I and II only" 13194139534794 true] [17592186310508 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534794 true] [17592186310508 1111 #uuid "eda4b349-f3ac-5703-b224-8300d536a6c6" 13194139534794 true] [17592186310509 1017 #edb/ref 17592186310510 13194139534794 true] [17592186310509 1089 "q-141086" 13194139534794 true] [17592186310509 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534794 true] [17592186310509 1100 "Consider the following differential equation.\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=-3y\n$$\n\n \n\nLet $f(x)=3{e}^{-x}.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\n- ${f}^{′}(x)=3{e}^{-x}$\n- Substituting $y=f(x)$ and ${y}^{′}={f}^{′}(x)$ into the differential equation gives a true statement\n- The function $y=f(x)$ is a solution of the differential equation" 13194139534794 true] [17592186310509 1113 #uuid "ca0e4ee1-6292-559e-9935-18a9adc4fe22" 13194139534794 true] [17592186310509 1145 "For a function $f(x)$ to be a solution to a differential equation, it must satisfy the equation for all values of $x$ in the equation's domain.\n\nWith that in mind, let's check each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is false. Differentiating $f(x)=3{e}^{-x},$ we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & ={(3{e}^{-x})}^{′} \\\\  & =-3{e}^{-x} \\\\  & \\ne 3{e}^{-x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement II is false. Substituting $y=3{e}^{-x}$ and ${y}^{′}=-3{e}^{-x}$ into the original equation, we get a false statement:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′} & \\overset{?}{=}-3y \\\\ -3{e}^{-x} & \\overset{?}{=}-3(3{e}^{-x}) \\\\ -3{e}^{-x} & \\ne -9{e}^{-x}\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement III is false. Since statement II is false, the function $y=3{e}^{-x}$ is not a solution to our differential equation.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"None.\"" 13194139534794 true] [17592186310510 1000 #edb/ref 17592186310511 13194139534794 true] [17592186310510 1000 #edb/ref 17592186310512 13194139534794 true] [17592186310510 1000 #edb/ref 17592186310513 13194139534794 true] [17592186310510 1000 #edb/ref 17592186310514 13194139534794 true] [17592186310510 1000 #edb/ref 17592186310515 13194139534794 true] [17592186310510 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534794 true] [17592186310510 1041 "selection" 13194139534794 true] [17592186310510 1104 #edb/ref 17592186310514 13194139534794 true] [17592186310510 1110 #uuid "0fd61664-dc80-5ee5-b6d5-ed8564b05673" 13194139534794 true] [17592186310511 1034 "II and III only" 13194139534794 true] [17592186310511 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534794 true] [17592186310511 1111 #uuid "7dd0170d-f326-58f5-9749-6c0c86a31a6e" 13194139534794 true] [17592186310512 1034 "I only" 13194139534794 true] [17592186310512 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534794 true] [17592186310512 1111 #uuid "786090ba-9cbf-54ea-a394-9daafec6aad5" 13194139534794 true] [17592186310513 1034 "III only" 13194139534794 true] [17592186310513 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534794 true] [17592186310513 1111 #uuid "b123aa26-72ff-5beb-b46d-3ca35327d703" 13194139534794 true] [17592186310514 1034 "None" 13194139534794 true] [17592186310514 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534794 true] [17592186310514 1111 #uuid "91713830-f892-5573-a648-0a2929a227e2" 13194139534794 true] [17592186310515 1034 "II only" 13194139534794 true] [17592186310515 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534794 true] [17592186310515 1111 #uuid "f65988d8-7b63-5a3f-868e-57f1ee94e5fe" 13194139534794 true] [17592186310516 1017 #edb/ref 17592186310517 13194139534794 true] [17592186310516 1089 "q-141108" 13194139534794 true] [17592186310516 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534794 true] [17592186310516 1100 "Consider the following initial value problem\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=-y,\\,y(0)=1.\n$$\n\nYou're given that $y=A{e}^{-x}$ is the solution to this initial value problem. What is the value of the constant $A?$" 13194139534794 true] [17592186310516 1113 #uuid "53021b4a-ecf6-51c5-9c2a-a4f9c53c3409" 13194139534794 true] [17592186310516 1145 "We're given that $y=A{e}^{-x}$ is the solution to the initial value problem. Therefore, it must satisfy the differential equation *and* the initial condition $y(0)=1.$\n\nSubstituting the initial condition $y(0)=1$ into our solution and solving for $A,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =A{e}^{-x} \\\\ 1 & =A{e}^{-0} \\\\ 1 & =A(1) \\\\ A & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the initial value problem is\n\n$$\ny=1{e}^{-x}={e}^{-x}.\n$$" 13194139534794 true] [17592186310517 1000 #edb/ref 17592186310518 13194139534794 true] [17592186310517 1000 #edb/ref 17592186310519 13194139534794 true] [17592186310517 1000 #edb/ref 17592186310520 13194139534794 true] [17592186310517 1000 #edb/ref 17592186310521 13194139534794 true] [17592186310517 1000 #edb/ref 17592186310522 13194139534794 true] [17592186310517 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534794 true] [17592186310517 1041 "selection" 13194139534794 true] [17592186310517 1104 #edb/ref 17592186310519 13194139534794 true] [17592186310517 1110 #uuid "021c376f-b348-53b0-90c8-42e126191cbb" 13194139534794 true] [17592186310518 1034 "2" 13194139534794 true] [17592186310518 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534794 true] [17592186310518 1111 #uuid "27ce4f98-69c1-5501-9df2-126de889fad5" 13194139534794 true] [17592186310519 1034 "1" 13194139534794 true] [17592186310519 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534794 true] [17592186310519 1111 #uuid "d496640d-5dc3-53d1-8063-49bf44149943" 13194139534794 true] [17592186310520 1034 "0" 13194139534794 true] [17592186310520 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534794 true] [17592186310520 1111 #uuid "da38b541-6ec6-5af7-b366-35bb89be2a83" 13194139534794 true] [17592186310521 1034 "-1" 13194139534794 true] [17592186310521 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534794 true] [17592186310521 1111 #uuid "223e5c53-9d6a-57a8-acdb-78b763a3f1ad" 13194139534794 true] [17592186310522 1034 "-2" 13194139534794 true] [17592186310522 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534794 true] [17592186310522 1111 #uuid "ffd20074-d614-5913-957c-3e6b685ffdc1" 13194139534794 true] [17592186310523 1017 #edb/ref 17592186310524 13194139534794 true] [17592186310523 1089 "q-141109" 13194139534794 true] [17592186310523 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534794 true] [17592186310523 1100 "Consider the following initial value problem\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=-2y,\\,y(0)=2.\n$$\n\nYou're given that $y=A{e}^{-2x}$ is the solution to this initial value problem. What is the value of the constant $A?$" 13194139534794 true] [17592186310523 1113 #uuid "7d075088-7ad8-5baf-a890-9be7b4897d61" 13194139534794 true] [17592186310523 1145 "We're given that $y=A{e}^{-2x}$ is the solution to the initial value problem. Therefore, it must satisfy the differential equation *and* the initial condition $y(0)=2.$\n\nSubstituting the initial condition $y(0)=2$ into our solution and solving for $A,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =A{e}^{-2x} \\\\ 2 & =A{e}^{-2(0)} \\\\ 2 & =A{e}^{0} \\\\ 2 & =A(1) \\\\ A & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the initial value problem is\n\n$$\ny=2{e}^{-2x}.\n$$" 13194139534794 true] [17592186310524 1000 #edb/ref 17592186310525 13194139534794 true] [17592186310524 1000 #edb/ref 17592186310526 13194139534794 true] [17592186310524 1000 #edb/ref 17592186310527 13194139534794 true] [17592186310524 1000 #edb/ref 17592186310528 13194139534794 true] [17592186310524 1000 #edb/ref 17592186310529 13194139534794 true] [17592186310524 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534794 true] [17592186310524 1041 "selection" 13194139534794 true] [17592186310524 1104 #edb/ref 17592186310525 13194139534794 true] [17592186310524 1110 #uuid "9d367f92-bd39-543c-a262-08c67e072c59" 13194139534794 true] [17592186310525 1034 "2" 13194139534794 true] [17592186310525 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534794 true] [17592186310525 1111 #uuid "ee5c774d-afee-57d7-84cf-a0112e0f4265" 13194139534794 true] [17592186310526 1034 "4" 13194139534794 true] [17592186310526 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534794 true] [17592186310526 1111 #uuid "5a5bf16a-f239-598e-9644-b30e5b4ee7de" 13194139534794 true] [17592186310527 1034 "0" 13194139534794 true] [17592186310527 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534794 true] [17592186310527 1111 #uuid "df57b554-74a6-5f0c-9daa-e52643a8a0cc" 13194139534794 true] [17592186310528 1034 "-1" 13194139534794 true] [17592186310528 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534794 true] [17592186310528 1111 #uuid "acdc6c56-2315-55fb-9644-96753e024035" 13194139534794 true] [17592186310529 1034 "-2" 13194139534794 true] [17592186310529 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534794 true] [17592186310529 1111 #uuid "6a024b94-cda4-5d3b-941c-aaf7e25ae8de" 13194139534794 true] [17592186310530 1017 #edb/ref 17592186310531 13194139534794